    67  /*
    68   Unfortunately aiNode has bone structures and meshes too, yet we can't assign
    69   the mesh to a bone aiNode as a skin may refer to several aiNodes. Therefore
    70   I've decided to import into this structure:
    71
    72     aiScene->mRootNode
    73      |        |->mMeshes (all the meshes)
    74      |        \->children (empty if there's no skeleton imported, no meshes)
    75      |             \->skeleton root aiNode*
    76      |                   |->bone aiNode
    77      |                   |   \->subbone aiNode
    78      |                   |->bone aiNode
    79      |                   |   ...
    80      |                   \->bone aiNode
    81      \->mMeshes[]
    82          \->aiBone, referencing mesh-less aiNodes from above
    83
    84    * - normally one, but if a model has several skeleton roots, then all of them
    85        are listed in aiScene->mRootNode->children, but all without meshes
    86  */
